# The one template whose text is not in the language it writes.
#
# `.prettierrc` gives every `*.jsonc.tpl` the jsonc parser, and this is the one
# file that cannot take it: `wrangler.jsonc`'s durable-object bindings and its
# `new_sqlite_classes` both break past the print width on a long tenant id, so
# both stay computed and arrive as block tokens — and `$DO_BINDINGS` standing
# where a JSON array's elements go is not JSON, however correct the file it
# renders. Named here rather than solved by dropping the rule, because the rule
# is right for a `.jsonc.tpl` without one.
#
# Nothing is unchecked as a result. `src/agent/formatting.spec.ts` runs the real
# prettier over the *rendered* `wrangler.jsonc` for every fixture and every
# sweep across the print width, which is the check that was ever load-bearing;
# what this file loses is format-on-save while editing it.
src/agent/templates/project/wrangler.jsonc.tpl
